/-!
# The patch `TrioFixNonLastOther2`: the pairs it puts back in order

`TrioFixNonLastOther2.lean` narrows Fix M, Fix G and change 1 of
`TrioFixNonLastOther.lean` (rules 1–10 of [koteitan/trio](https://github.com/koteitan/trio)
with Fixes A–E, N, G, M).  `x2Of` is this patch, `xOf` is `TrioFixNonLastOther`, `allOf`
is `TrioRulesAll` (before `TrioFixNonLastOther`).

* **The review's nine pairs**: in order under `allOf` and `x2Of`, out of order under
  `xOf`.
* **What stays**: the 27 BMS expansions `M(P+t·ω)[n] = M(P+t·(n+1))` (`n = 1, 2`) and
  change 4's `M(Ω_{Ω_ω}+Ω_Ω+Ω_{ω·2})[n] = M(Ω_{Ω_ω}+Ω_Ω+Ω_{ω+n+1})`; three calibrated
  families keep the counts of `TrioFixNonLastOtherSheet.lean` (the other two are in
  `TrioFixNonLastOther2SheetHeavy1.lean`).
* **Against `TrioRulesAll`**: eight families; `brokenFixed` counts the pairs in order
  under `allOf` and out of order under `x2Of` (0 after `Ω_{Ω_2}`, `Ω_{Ω_3}`, `Ω_{Ω_4}`,
  `Ω_{Ω+1}`, `Ω_{Ω_{Ω+1}}`, `Ω_{Ω_{ω·2}}`; 8 after `Ω_{Ω_{ω^2}}`, 6 after
  `Ω_{Ω_{ω+1}}`) and the other way round.  Four heavier families are in
  `TrioFixNonLastOther2SheetHeavy2.lean`.

Standardness (yaBMS `bms -s`) is checked outside Lean: no matrix that is standard under
`allOf` becomes non-standard under `x2Of` in these families.  All of it is `#guard`s: a
calibration, not a theorem.  About 140 seconds for a check.
-/

namespace Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioFixNonLastOther2

open Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRules
open Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRules2
open Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRulesNL
